{
  "case_id": "2007-06-766",
  "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "New York State Board of Elections",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "For 10 years, New York relied on political party primaries to nominate general election candidates for supreme court justice, but that process discouraged qualified candidates and spawned unseemly, expensive, and potentially corrupting fundraising by judicial candidates."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Just focus on, if you would, Mr. Olson, on the election for the delegates. Now, suppose it were shown -- a hypothetical case -- that it's extremely difficult to get on that ballot. You need, let's say, 2,000 signatures in 30 days. Would there be a constitutional issue raised by that situation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "New York County Democratic Committee",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 17,
        "start": 17
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I'd like to begin by responding to Justice Kennedy's question regarding the election of delegates and fairness for voters. There are two responses: In this case that I have -- this case, there was conceded below that the requirement for delegates of getting only 500 signatures was no barrier at all."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rossman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0000",
      "kind": "allegation",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There's evidence that there's legislative intent that, in fact, candidates not appear at the convention because it would be unseemly for them to do so."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well then, how are the delegates to find out the qualifications? In other words, if that's the intent of this statute, then you have a statute that's designed on the one hand to have convention delegates who will choose, and on the other hand to prevent the convention delegates from finding out the qualifications of the different applicants, in which case it would seem to be a statute that would give the actual power of selection to the leader or the chairman -- I forget the title -- of the Democratic Party."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rossman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0002",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "where the political leaders, through their structure, do pick the candidates, for example in the case of vacancy election, which this Court upheld as constitutional in the Rodriquez case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "the parties",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "the parties themselves, through what we contend is core associational activity protected by the First Amendment, participate in their own way of choosing in educating delegates and in putting forth the candidacies of judicial -- potential judicial nominees."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Rossman",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the evidence in this case is that rank-and-file voters are not educated hardly at all about the judge candidates that they select."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if the autonomy of the party and, let's say, the leader is the justification for this, the party -- how -- how autonomous can a party be when it's told, even if you want to be more democratic about how you choose your candidates, you can't because New York is forcing this system on you?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What about the burden on a single delegate wanting to be on the ballot? I think that requires 500 votes, and there was no specific finding that that was burden, was there? Or am incorrect?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But Storer --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: May I ask you this\nquestion, Mr. Schwarz. Supposing that the statute did\nnot contain the delegate-selection process and instead,\nsaid: Delegates shall be selected by the county\nchairman in each county and by the organization. Would\nit then be unconstitutional?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Board of Elections",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "could use something that the Board of Elections' brief\nconceded in both their reply and their opening brief,\nthey said a person -- they said that party members who\nwanted to attempt to assemble a slate to try to\ninfluence the decision at the convention would be \"well\nserved\" -- that's their exact words -- to assemble and\nrun a slate."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: If I could interrupt,\nJustice Breyer, for just a moment. But in the Minnesota\ncase the thumb on the scale was to deprive the\nconstituents of a First Amendment right."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Souter",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOUTER: No, but what you are\ncalling -- and correct me if I am wrong. Maybe I\nmisunderstand this. I think what you are calling the\nsevere burden is the difficulty of assembling a whole\nslate that can control the meeting or have a majority in\nthe ultimate meeting of that delegate, of those\ndelegates, and therefore actually select the candidate\nwho wants to put the slate together."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2007-06-766",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b5f3c1d779fe28bddbf408cd1079340a63965bea2abb833dda78f75ec74d204",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b5f3c1d779f-0002-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
